          deckDescription: 'Two standard 52-card decks combined (104 cards) plus four jokers (108 cards total). Four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), thirteen ranks each in duplicate. Jokers and twos are wild; used for Biriba (Brazilian rummy) with sequence and set building.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs) in duplicate. Sequences must be in the same suit; jokers and twos may substitute for any card. Sets are three or four of the same rank in any suits.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit in each deck (ace through two). Jokers and twos are wild. Standard rummy ranking for sequences (ace high or low as house rules); the first to go out with valid melds wins the hand.',
          dealPattern: 'Cards are dealt individually anti-clockwise.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; points are determined by individual card values and biriba completeness.',
          rankingSystem: 'Canasta-style points',
          useTrump: false,
          notApplicableReasons: {
            specialCards: 'Jokers and 2s act as wildcards in melds; modeled in meld logic.',
            shedding: 'Goal is to go out by melding and discarding; not a race to empty hand in the shedding sense.',
            fishingConfig: 'Biriba uses draw-and-discard and melds, not a capture-from-tableau fishing mechanic.',
          },
        },
        synthesis: {
          hero: {
            title: 'BIRIBA',
            subtitle: "Greece's Favourite Rummy Game",
            tagline: 'Build your melds. Complete your biriba. Go out in style.',
          },
          shortDescription: "The most popular card game in Greece. A rich partnership rummy where you build sets and runs, race to complete 7-card 'biribas', and grab reserve hands from the pot. Two decks, four Jokers, endless strategy. Clean biribas score 500; dirty ones 300. First team to the target wins.",
          uiThemes: [
